Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: set exception TID before reconstructing QoS headers

NSS MCBC exceptions bypass REO and therefore have no REO-populated rxcb TID.
Read it from the packet descriptor before undecapsulation, so mac80211 uses
the original QoS TID for duplicate and CCMP/GCMP replay checks. Both normal
and mesh NSS MCBC delivery use this entry point.

The host NULL queue descriptor path has the same ordering problem: it sets
TID only after MPDU processing has already reconstructed the QoS header.
Move that assignment before processing without weakening PN validation.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -3463,6 +3463,9 @@
 	bool fast_rx = false;
 
 	rxcb = ATH11K_SKB_RXCB(msdu);
 
+	/* This exception bypasses REO's population of the receive TID. */
+	rxcb->tid = ath11k_dp_rx_h_mpdu_start_tid(ar->ab, rxcb->rx_desc);
+
 	ath11k_dp_rx_h_ppdu(ar, rxcb->rx_desc, &rx_status);
 	ath11k_dp_rx_h_mpdu(ar, msdu, rxcb->rx_desc, &rx_status, &fast_rx, true);
@@ -5061,10 +5064,9 @@
 	}
 	ath11k_dp_rx_h_ppdu(ar, desc, status);
 
+	rxcb->tid = ath11k_dp_rx_h_mpdu_start_tid(ar->ab, desc);
 	fast_rx = false;
 	ath11k_dp_rx_h_mpdu(ar, msdu, desc, status, &fast_rx, false);
 
-	rxcb->tid = ath11k_dp_rx_h_mpdu_start_tid(ar->ab, desc);
-
 	/* Please note that caller will having the access to msdu and completing
 	 * rx with mac80211. Need not worry about cleaning up amsdu_list.
